    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "I used to think a wedding was a simple affair. A boy and girl meet, they fall in love, he buys a ring, she buys a dress, they say \"I do.\" I was wrong. That's getting married. A wedding is an entirely different proposition. I know. I've just been through one. Not my own."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 1,
        "line": 862,
        "text": "Oh."
      }
